+			"lines": "658-695",
+			"claim": "runTools builds toolsByName from the current lane configuration filtered by the persisted activeToolNames, i.e. exactly the current declaration set recovery must re-check."
+		},
+		{
+			"path": "packages/agent/src/harness/execution/tools.ts",
+			"lines": "130-160",
+			"claim": "executeToolCall dereferences call.tool.execute inside its try block, which is why a missing declaration surfaced as a TypeError-derived error result instead of an interruption."
+		},
+		{
+			"path": "packages/agent/src/harness/pico3/kinds/tool.ts",
+			"lines": "128-158",
+			"claim": "The experimental pico3 kernel already encodes the intended rule on recovery (`if (cp.replay !== \"safe\" || (declaration.replay ?? \"unsafe\") !== \"safe\")` and a separate missing-declaration branch); the drive runtime is the implementation that violated it."
+		}
+	],
+	"validation": {
+		"command": "node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs",
+		"status": "passed",
+		"notes": "The regression loads the real production modules through .prale-eval/subject.mjs createGraph (drive/tools.ts plus the lane, restore, tool-placement, progress, execution and session modules it links against) and fakes only the boundary: the pi-ai argument validator, uuidv7, and the chord context helpers. It rebuilds a reopened durable tool batch exactly as the kernel persists it (assistant message with tool-call blocks, operation meta/state with effect_pending calls, persisted operationToolArgs and pendingToolOutput checkpoints) and runs runTools on it. Scenarios: (1) persisted replay:\"safe\" with the declaration gone -> asserts the tool never runs, no recovery tool_start is emitted, and the result carries the durable snapshot 'durable partial' plus the interruption marker and its details; (2) declaration downgraded to replay:\"never\" -> same interrupted settlement, zero executions; (3) declaration with no replay field (default not safe) -> interrupted with marker only and no invented details; (4) control: both policies safe -> the effect replays exactly once with the persisted arguments and publishes the real result with one recovery tool_start; (5) persisted replay:\"never\" with a now-safe declaration -> interrupted, because the durable policy cannot be upgraded; (6) mixed batch (missing + downgraded) -> both settle interrupted and are placed in source order. Verified both directions: with the fix the script exits 0, and with the original line `if (!cancelled && call.replay === \"safe\")` restored it exits 1 with AssertionError 'missing declaration: the result must report an interrupted tool execution, got: TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading \\'execute\\')'; a partial fix that only guards the missing declaration also fails it ('declaration downgraded to never: the tool effect ran even though the call must not replay'). Runtime is ~0.15s, no dependencies or network. Limitation: node_modules is absent in this checkout, so the repo